uid_gid_lookup.c: reject the undefined id as a 32-bit number whatever the
signedness of id_t.

ACL_UNDEFINED_ID is ((id_t)-1).  get_id() compares it with the unsigned
long it parsed; with an unsigned 32-bit id_t that is 4294967295, the value
meant, but the LikeOS libc's id_t is a signed int, and -1 widened to
unsigned long is 2^64-1, which no 32-bit id equals: "4294967295" would be
taken as a user or group id.  Comparing with the id converted to uid_t
first gives 4294967295 with either id_t.

